<p>Sorry for the late reply</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Reply</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide&nbsp;Reply</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I see what you mean with overall clinical tone, I will begin to update such with help from others.</p>
<p>Crabs: Overall I was aiming to connect the crabs with the cancer constellation through the dates of the journal entries being the day that the constellation is represented to the end date that it is represented, I believe I can make this more evident however.</p>
<p>Diary Pages: I see what you mean, overall I was aiming to do a slow progression into hatred of the art, but it appears it wasn’t visible, I assume having a distinct part where it appears to be teetering into hatred would make it easier? Overall I presume a reworking would help?</p>
<p>Overall the subtle hatred throughout should be a bit more evident instead of just a random outburst at the end after such a rework.</p>
<p>Or I could frame it as more of a perfected finished product and his death can be more concretely as a byproduct of overworking, and scheele’s green.</p>
<p>Also I aimed to leave the artist’s death to user interpretation either scheele’s green as you mentioned or the first activation of SCP-XXXX-1. The death’s contents can change depending on what the final few diary entries indicate I presume.</p>
</div>
