<p>Collapsed for ease of scrolling.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Crabs: Overall I was aiming to connect the crabs with the cancer constellation through the dates of the journal entries being the day that the constellation is represented to the end date that it is represented, I believe I can make this more evident however.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Then how would the constellation’s prevalence relate to the art and the artist’s rage? That seems like another tenuous connection.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Diary Pages: I see what you mean, overall I was aiming to do a slow progression into hatred of the art, but it appears it wasn’t visible, I assume having a distinct part where it appears to be teetering into hatred would make it easier? Overall I presume a reworking would help?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If anything, I’d almost recommend leaning into his self-assurance that this will be his masterpiece. I think you’d be able to make it clear that he dislikes it through over-enthusiastic optimism, if that makes sense.</p>
<p>I have to say, I’m a little confused when it comes to the bit about the paint not sticking to the painting. Is that a motif I’m not getting, or something about the paint that I missed?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also I aimed to leave the artist’s death to user interpretation either scheele’s green as you mentioned or the first activation of SCP-XXXX-1. The death’s contents can change depending on what the final few diary entries indicate I presume.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I can appreciate the meaningful ambiguity, but at the moment, the ending entry feels a tad anti-climactic. I think that a more carefully handled progression of self-hatred might help with that.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

